<SizeGuide
  title="Adidas Size Guide — Does Adidas Run Big? (Charts & Tips) | Attirel"
  description="Adidas shoes tend to run about half a size large — the opposite of Nike. Full Adidas apparel charts with US/UK/EU conversions and model-by-model shoe tips."
  brand="Adidas"
  verdictQuestion="Does Adidas run big?"
  charts={charts}
>
  <Fragment slot="verdict">
    <strong>In footwear, yes — Adidas tends to run about half a size large</strong>, especially
    Originals like the Superstar, Stan Smith, and Samba, so many people go down half a size.
    (That's the opposite of Nike.) Apparel is broadly true to size with a slightly relaxed
    European athletic cut.
  </Fragment>
  <Fragment slot="tips">
    <li><strong>Originals (Superstar, Stan Smith, Samba, Gazelle):</strong> run large — go down half a size from your measured size.</li>
    <li><strong>Ultraboost and running styles:</strong> fit snugger and true — stay with your measured size.</li>
    <li><strong>Soccer shoes and cleats:</strong> designed to fit tight to the foot — true to size for a performance fit, half up for comfort.</li>
    <li><strong>Switching from Nike?</strong> The adjustments stack: if you size up half in Nike, you may drop a full size coming to Adidas Originals.</li>
    <li><strong>Track pants and jackets:</strong> classic cuts run roomy — size down for a slimmer look, or check the "slim" / "tapered" labels.</li>
  </Fragment>
</SizeGuide>
